From b6a598373e1b9897cc712c6ba92358abb5275487 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BearddOddity <beardedoddity@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 07:10:55 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 09/13] Mod-API: known limits as they stand - the trail lies on
 the floor and goes round walls; places last for the scene; a module's words
 are its own

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 bible/06-Systems/Mod-API.md | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/bible/06-Systems/Mod-API.md b/bible/06-Systems/Mod-API.md
index 15404916fc..6093c32696 100644
--- a/bible/06-Systems/Mod-API.md
+++ b/bible/06-Systems/Mod-API.md
@@ -140,8 +140,11 @@ The game binds F5 (character sheet), F6 (inventory), F8 (screenshot), F9/F11 (qu
   The standalone dungeon page (`?shot` probes) does not announce `drawFx`: it is a test host, not one a player boots.
 - A module sees the compass's mark, which is the quest's place (the tracked quest, a place the player's map holds) and, inside a
   dungeon or building, the Exact Quest-guidance tier's marks; it is never told a place the game would not already show.
-- `guide-trail`'s quest path is a straight line at the player's own height: a module cannot read the game's terrain, so on a
-  hillside it can float above or sink below the ground, and a wall hides the part you cannot see.
+- The guide trail plans over the world probe (`floor`, `ray`, `doors`, `known`): it lies on the floor and the terrain and goes
+  round walls, but it only knows the way between a dungeon's floors that the player's map has recorded, and where the mark is
+  shut inside a building it leads to the nearest door (the street's door list), not through it.
+- Pins and destinations last for the scene: a door, a dungeon or a travel clears them (each place has its own frame).
+- A module's own words (`dfo.say`) are its own: the handle has no text core for a module author yet.
 
 ## PINNED
 
